# Pinned toolchain that generates requirements.txt. NOT a runtime dependency of
# this role -- nothing here is installed on a controller or a managed host.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `pip-compile --generate-hashes` output depends on more than pip-tools' own
# version. Its header is rendered by Click, and Click changed the default of a
# flag option between releases:
#
#   click 8.4.1 -> cli.params['no_index'].default is False
#   click 8.5.0 -> cli.params['no_index'].default is Sentinel.UNSET
#
# piptools/utils.py::get_compile_command skips an option when
# `option.default == value`. Under 8.4.1 that guard fires and `--no-index` is
# omitted; under 8.5.0 `Sentinel.UNSET == False` is False, the guard does not
# fire, and the flag is printed although it was never passed. Same pip-tools,
# same inputs, two different headers.
#
# Pinning pip-tools alone therefore does NOT make regeneration reproducible,
# because `pip install pip-tools==7.6.1` admits either Click. The whole
# generator toolchain is pinned here instead, pip included -- pip is the
# resolver, and the python:3.11-slim tag is mutable, so the base image's
# bundled pip is not a fixed input either.
#
# REGENERATING THIS FILE (rarely; only to move the toolchain deliberately):
#
#   docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 -v "$PWD:/w" -w /w python:3.11-slim \
#     sh -c 'pip install -q pip-tools==7.6.1 click==8.5.0 && \
#            pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe \
#              --output-file=requirements-generator.txt requirements-generator.in'
#
# This is a fixed point: installing requirements-generator.txt and re-running
# the command above reproduces requirements-generator.txt byte for byte.
pip-tools==7.6.1
click==8.5.0
